# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/skinning
title Skinning 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Ironforge

# Skinning 1-300 for both factions: for each skill band, a loop the arrow walks
# through the densest camps of skinnable beasts of the right level (expected
# skill-ups per yard of a lap, with the time to kill and skin each beast), at the
# lowest character level that keeps the loop nearly as good: no beast or other
# creature on it more than a level above that level, and away from the other
# faction's towns. Skill needed: 1 for level 10 and below, (level-10)x10 for
# 11-20, level x5 above 20. Beast lists per zone are curated
# (tools/lib/professions/gathering/skinning.js); levels and spawns come from
# npcs.json, and what a skinning gives from players' recorded gathers.
#
# Herb and ore spawns come from the Forever TrinityCore world DB (its spawn pools
# say how often each is up); beast spawns and levels from the reference data;
# trainer learn skills and prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists; recipes
# and their skill colours from the Forever client tables.
# Zones are ranked for a character of a fifth of the band's skill in levels (at
# least 5; ASSUMED: one levelling with the profession); a loop that asks more
# says so with a `level` goal, and loses half its worth per level it asks above.
# Ranks ask no character level: Forever's sniffed trainer lists carry none for
# Herbalism, Mining or Skinning, and players' recordings show Expert Mining
# trained at 15 and Artisan Skinning at 29.
# Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine converts them where Forever
# changed a map frame, and a map without an Era frame (Zephras Isle) compiles live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice
section Skinning 1-50

step Learn Skinning
  tip Any Skinning trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Skinning at any level (10c), and so does the Junior Skinning Trainer in each starting area; the arrow picks the nearest. Buy a Skinning Knife from a trade goods or general vendor: keep it in your bags, you cannot skin without it. The first-hour quest of each starting area (Rascally Rodents, Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery, The Woodland Protector, Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise, A Humble Task, Marla's Last Wish) offers Pelt Collecting for Beginners as a reward: reading it gives 2 skill, up to 15. Trade goods vendors and the junior trainers sell the Apprentice's Skinning Satchel, a four-slot bag for leather and hides (25c). If you sat at your starting area's campfire for The Great Outdoors, the camping guide there also offers Camping 101: Skinning: hand it in to the skinning trainer it names once you reach skill 20, for the Camp Chair recipe.
  train Skinning Apprentice
  buy 7005 x1 nearest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Skinning 1-50

step Beasts 1-5 (1-50)
  tip Walk the loop and kill and skin Battleboar (3), Crag Boar (5), Duskbat (1), Juvenile Snow Leopard (5), Juvenile Vuldren (1), Mangy Duskbat (3), Mangy Nightsaber (2), Mangy Wolf (4), Mottled Boar (1), Mountain Cougar (3), Plainstrider (1), Ragged Timber Wolf (2), Ragged Young Wolf (1), Scorpid Worker (3), Scrawny Ursera (3), Small Crag Boar (3), Thistle Boar (2), Timber Wolf (2), Ursera Scavenger (4), Young Black Bear (5), Young Nightsaber (1), Young Thistle Boar (1), Young Wolf (1) until Skinning 50; loot each corpse, then skin it, and skin the highest-level beasts your skill allows. A beast of level L needs skill (L-10)x10 up to level 20 and Lx5 above. Quests in these zones need Skinning: Gathering Leather (level 8, Veren Tallstrider, Mulgore; Horde), Rough Wolf Pelts (level 8, Helene Peltskinner, Elwynn Forest; Alliance). The arrow takes the loop that gets you there soonest from where you are and walks it until the skill is reached; each loop keeps to creatures no more than a level above you and away from the other faction's towns, and the window names it and its lap. Expect about 60 beasts for these 49 points: about 60 Ruined Leather Scraps.
